From: Yanan He <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] common/device-utils: include libgen.h for basename()

With musl libc, basename() is only declared in <libgen.h>; <string.h>
does not expose the GNU non-POSIX variant. Recent clang treats the
resulting implicit declaration / int-to-pointer assignment as a hard
error (-Wint-conversion), causing the build to fail:

    common/device-utils.c:344:7: error: incompatible integer to
        pointer conversion assigning to 'char *' from 'int'
        [-Wint-conversion]
        name = basename(path);

Add the missing include so basename() has its proper prototype.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [musl/clang build fix]
---
 common/device-utils.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/common/device-utils.c
+++ b/common/device-utils.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include <blkid/blkid.h>
 #include <linux/limits.h>
 #include <linux/fs.h>
+#include <libgen.h>
 #include <limits.h>
 #include "kernel-lib/sizes.h"
 #include "kernel-shared/disk-io.h"
